# Plain language writing

Use this for descriptions, explanations, comments, commit messages, PR text, and any user-facing copy. Code syntax is unchanged (types, operators, and required punctuation stay as the language needs).

## Voice

- Sound human. Clear, concise, honest.
- Short sentences. Casual grammar is fine.
- Keep every must-keep detail. Cut the rest.

## Do not use

- Hype and filler ("dive into", "unleash", "game-changing", "robust", "seamless", "leverage")
- Rhetorical questions and engagement bait ("Ready to get started?", "Let's explore")
- Weak openers or closers ("Basically", "Clearly", "Interestingly")
- "X and also Y" padding

## Punctuation in prose

- Prefer periods and commas over em dashes and colons in user-facing sentences.
- Bullet lists in technical docs are fine when they aid scanning.

## When unsure

Ask a short clarifying question instead of guessing.
